# VRoid material names

## Source vs workflow

| | Example |
|---|---------|
| **Source** (VRoid import, until Phase B) | `N00_000_00_Face_00_SKIN (Instance)` |
| **Workflow** (pipeline scripts) | `Face_Skin` |

Phase B stores `scene["vroid_material_rename_map"]` (`source → workflow`).

Class suffixes (`-NoRim.NoOutline`) are separate — see `mtoon-material-classes` rule. Identity never uses `.` (only `_`). Texture slug = `identity.lower()` → `face_skin`.

## Standardization rule

1. Strip `N{xx}_{xxx}_{slot}_` import prefix and ` (Instance)`
2. VRoid `_00_` is a **category separator** → `_` + Title Case (`Face_00_SKIN` → `Face_Skin`)
3. `_00_FACE` category → `{Feature}_Face` (e.g. `FaceMouth` → `Mouth_Face`). `_00_EYE` → `{Feature}_Eye` (e.g. `EyeIris_00_EYE` → `Iris_Eye`, `EyeHighlight_00_EYE` → `EyeHighlight_Eye`). Other: `Face_00_SKIN` → `Face_Skin`
4. Clothing `_01_CLOTH` → `{Item}_Cloth`; strip optional `Accessory_` prefix (`Accessory_RabbitEar_01_CLOTH` → `RabbitEar_Cloth`); layered → `{ItemAlias}_{NN}_Cloth` (e.g. `Hoodie_01_Cloth`)

